      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We have investigated the potential for contrast-enhanced near-infrared fluorescence imaging of tissue on a mobile phone platform. Charge-coupled device- and phone-based cameras were used to image molded and three-dimensional-printed tissue phantoms, and an ex vivo animal model. Quantitative and qualitative evaluations of image quality demonstrate the viability of this approach and elucidate variations in performance due to wavelength, pixel color, and image processing."},
